   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to authorizing those who\nare within a year of fulfilling the minimum age or education prerequisites for\na competitive class civil service position to sit for the civil service test\nassociated with that role",
    "basePrintNo": "S8216",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8216-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §54, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8216\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the civil service law, in relation to authorizing those\nwho are within a year of fulfilling the minimum age or education prereq-\nuisites for a competitive class civil service position to sit for the\ncivil service test associated with that role\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo permit individuals within twelve months of meeting the minimum age or\neducational qualifications for a competitive class civil service role to\ntake the civil service examination for that position.\n\n \nSUMMARY:\n\nSection 1: Allows individuals within twelve months of meeting the mini-\nmum age or education requirements for a competitive class civil service\nposition to take a civil service exam for such position.\n\nSection 2: The effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn the past decade, the erosion of the public sector workforce in New\nYork State has reached crisis levels. While public sector employers look\nto fill the gaps in employment, they are hamstringed by the lengthy\nprocess to recruit, test, and onboard into a civil service position. The\ncurrent hiring process for civil service jobs, which starts with taking\nan exam and ends with being hired, can take up to 6 months. To combat\nthis lengthy process, this bill allows individuals that are within 12\nmonths of meeting the age or education requirements of a given civil\nservice job to take an exam for that position. Doing so allows prospec-\ntive employees to get their foot in the door early, reducing the time\nthey need to wait between meeting the job requirements and beginning a\ncareer in the public sector.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect Immediately.\n",
